1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,616
The Room tab lays out every cabinet in the kitchen.

2
00:00:07,616 --> 00:00:14,055
Set the room: 144" wide, 120" deep, 96" walls.

3
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:18,564
Arrange along the back wall lines the cabinets up for you.

4
00:00:18,564 --> 00:00:32,888
Scroll to zoom and drag to orbit around the 3D room.

5
00:00:32,888 --> 00:00:36,926
Plan view: looking down, back wall at the top, fronts marked with a thick line.

6
00:00:36,926 --> 00:00:44,307
The 36" wall cabinet belongs over the sink. Drag W1 out of the way...

7
00:00:44,307 --> 00:00:51,725
...drag W2 into the corner over the sink...

8
00:00:51,725 --> 00:00:59,937
...and W1 back beside it. Snap butts the cabinets together and lines them up.

9
00:00:59,937 --> 00:01:04,052
Elevation: the back wall face-on, with the sizes and heights off the floor.

10
00:01:04,052 --> 00:01:12,381
Click a cabinet to change it right here. Make B2 a 4-drawer base.

11
00:01:12,381 --> 00:01:20,597
Edit opens the full cabinet editor; Done brings you back to the room.

12
00:01:20,597 --> 00:01:35,797
Back in 3D, the finished layout: bases, uppers over the sink, and the pantry.
